Sun Aug 30 17:13:35 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to version 0.9.5:
  * Rework sample block reading; warn when the sample consumption rate
    drops below the configured sample rate
  * Honour the value of -unique; -unique=false previously still
    enabled the filter
  * Only SIGINT is handled now, not SIGTERM, so systemctl stop or kill
    skips the graceful shutdown and can truncate a -samplefile dump
  * Switch logging from log to log/slog
  * Raise the documented minimum Go version to 1.21
  * Update the compatible-meter tables, adding the Itron 100WR
- Add rtlamr-no-debug-stdout-print.patch, a backport of upstream commit
  a1f6df8: 0.9.5 printed the build dir to stdout, corrupting the first
  line of csv/json output; the fix is one commit past v0.9.5 and is not
  in any release yet
- Regenerate vendor.tar.gz; the vendored module set is unchanged
- Build with the go-modules idiom (go build -mod=vendor -buildmode=pie
  -trimpath) instead of the golang-packaging macros
- Add %check running the upstream test suite
- License is AGPL-3.0-only AND BSD-2-Clause AND BSD-3-Clause; vendored
  rtltcp grants no or-later upgrade, r900/gf and x/xerrors are
  BSD-3-Clause, pkg/errors is BSD-2-Clause
- _service: go_modules and download_files to manual (Factory rejects
  trylocal), drop the no-op set_version

